# Tool authoring rules

Applies when editing `tools/**` or `lib/tools/**`.

## New tool checklist

**Preferred — config-driven:**

1. Create `tools/config/your-slug.config.ts` (copy from existing config)
2. Add slug to `configSlugs` in `lib/tools/registry.ts`
3. Run `npm run validate:tools && npm run build`

**Legacy — component-driven:**

1. `lib/tools/[name]/calculate.ts` — pure functions
2. `tools/[slug]/[PascalCase]Tool.tsx` — `"use client"`, wraps `ToolTemplate`
3. Entry in `componentRegistrations` inside `lib/tools/registry.ts`

## ToolTemplate props (required)

```tsx
<ToolTemplate
  path={`/tools/${metadata.slug}`}
  title={metadata.title}
  description={metadata.description}
  category={categoryName}
  relatedTools={relatedTools}
  onSubmit={handleSubmit}
  inputArea={...}
  calculate={{ label: "Calculate" }}
  resultsEmpty={!result}
  resultsArea={...}
  appCta={{ title: "...", description: "..." }}  // tool-specific
  faq={[...]}  // min 3 items
/>
```

## Validation pattern

- Validate in `handleSubmit`; set field errors; `return` early
- Call `calculate*()` from lib — never inline formulas in TSX
- Show comparisons/trivia in results area (amber callout pattern)

## Do not

- Register `tools/_template/` — copy only
- Pass functions through server→client props (metadata only)
- Duplicate SEO metadata in tool TSX files

See `docs/ENGINEERING_PLAYBOOK.md` §4 for full spec.
